<title>TURKEY: Turkish Aksa 9-mth profits up 112 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Aksa 9-mth profits up 112 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	1,178.37  vs   1,055.74</p>
<p>    Net profit			 3,933.76  vs   1,854.94</p>
<p>    Net sales			 18,743.12  vs  12,883.30</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 4,949.30  vs   2,747.85</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     1,778.14  vs     885.30</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense		331.37  vs     282.25</p>
<p>    Interest paid			312.61  vs     173.71</p>
<p>    Total debts			5,648.10  vs   5,689.70</p>
<p>    Equity			    11,387.07  vs   5,289.93</p>
<p>    Capital			    3,338.30  vs   1,757.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Acrylic based tow and fibre producer Aksa Akrilik Kimya Sanayii A.S. is owned largely by Akkok textile group and textile producer Altinyildiz Mensucat.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875 EKS</p>
</text>
